ause at the  beginning of the season will and eleven  are now living in california with eleven  struggling to fit in this is the first  time she's ever been educated in a  public setting rather than being  homeschooled by hopper or in a secret  experimental lab matters get worse  however when she runs a foul of valley  girl queen bee angela angela and her  posse relentlessly bully 11 now going by  her birth name jane which given 11's  latent telekinetic powers makes the  parallels between 11 and carrie all the  more clear when she gets bullied at a  roller rink one of the bullies even  pours a milkshake all over her in a  scene directly calling back to the image  of carrie doused in pig's blood however  the climax of this plotline where she  doesn't go on a telekinetic rampage  seems to be a purposeful inversion by  the duffers  wes cravens a nightmare on elm street  from 1984 is a classic horror film for a  reason it starred robert england as  freddy krueger the iconic knife-fingered  hat and sweater-wearing child killer who  was killed in an act of vigilante  justice and came back as a dream demon  murdering the children of the people who  killed him while ostensibly a slasher  film it is elevated by england's  committed performance craven's dreamlike  direction and the cool gory kills  please god this  god  season four of stranger things revels in  a nightmare on elm street references the  villain uses the fears and anxieties of  teens to kill them even the bloody  deaths of his victims floating in the  air is reminiscent of the first death in  the original nightmare film as well as  the plot about a perceived troublemaker  being framed for the murder however the  main easter egg is the duffer brothers  casting england in the series he plays  victor creel a prisoner who as a younger  man in the 1950s was framed for killing  his children he puts in a great  performance even if it's a more  sympathetic one rather than the  villainous work you might expect  the popular tabletop role-playing game  dungeons and dragons or dmd has always  been a big part of stranger things in  fact the pilot episode opens with the  main quartet mike dustin lucas and will  playing the rpg it even plays a pivotal  role in the characters defeating the  villains of the upside down throughout  the series this includes helping them  understand the fourth season's new  villain which they've dubbed vecna based  on a wizard who harnesses the powers of  a dark realm however being said in the  80s it means that the show is finally  tackling the satanic panic of the era  during this time certain activities like  playing dungeons and dragons were  considered legitimately evil in a  supernatural sense this was spurred on  by a growing evangelical movement during  the conservative reagan administration  the artist jack chick of the infamous  chick tracks comics was an acolyte of  both extreme evangelicalism and  conservatism and immediately jumped on  the anti-d and d bandwagon he wrote and  drew the strip dark dungeons where a  girl uses spells she learned from d to  control people in episode 2 of season 4  basketball star jason whose girlfriend  eddie was framed for killing retells  nearly the same hypothetical about why  eddie a known d d player is dangerous  eddie munson  he's a part of that freak devil called  hellfire  at the end of season three of stranger  things viewers saw hopper get blown up  during the last episode sacrificing  himself in an attempt to stop the  encroaching upside down however we also  got a tantalizing after credit scene  that hinted that he might be alive in a  russian prison this means that season 4  deals with joyce and murray attempting  to find and rescue hopper from the  soviet union this is set in motion when  they find what looks like a ransom note  and a phone number to call when they  dial the number they get in touch with  the russian who claims he can get hopper  to safety for a price however when joyce  initially calls